  "body": "**Stacked on #603** (#330, the face-lay rows, which also carries #593 and #573). Review only this PR's own commit, `e14ee4a2`.\n\n#606 left three items to decide. Each is recorded in `docs/decisions/606-align-pivot.md`, with what was considered and dropped.\n\n## 1. The typed-angle Apply turns about the WCS origin, with a choice\n- **Default pivot: the setup's WCS origin.** That is the WCS entity's position, or zero if none is placed, read the same way as `posting::wcs_context`. The part point on the origin stays on it, which answers the maintainer's report that alignment \"shifts the model relative to the origin\".\n- **Angles stay absolute from \"as modelled\".** Re-applying the same angles is refused (\"already holds the part that way\") rather than drifting. All-zero means \"as modelled\".\n- **The choice:** an `about [WCS origin | part centre]` combo sits beside Apply, and the tooltip names the pivot. \"Part centre\" is the old behaviour.\n- **Presets (Flip over X, Turn Z 90, …) still turn about the part centre,** and their tooltip says so. About the origin, a flip would put a part sitting on Z 0 under the table.\n- **Code:** new `crates/app/src/setup_turn.rs` and `AlignPartToSetup::turn(…, pivot)`. `CommandKind::AlignPart` gains `pivot`. It is still **one undoable command**.\n\n## 2. Lay on a plane defaults to face down (maintainer's call: recommended option taken)\n- The face row's \"Flip\" becomes **\"Face down\"**, on for a new pick: the picked face sits on the plane with the part on top. The points row's \"Flip points\" becomes **\"Points down\"**, also on by default.\n- **Only the UI draft default changed.** `PlaneLay::flip` keeps its meaning for the app, MCP and scripts.\n- **Saved setups store the resulting transform, so old projects load and post identically.**\n\n## 3. The structural test checks the pane, not the window\n- `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure` now asserts every alignment control, including the new combo and Apply, lies inside the **properties pane's tab rect**.\n- Putting the face row back on one line (the #330 regression) **fails** the test: `\"Face down\" … [[1349.8 344] - [1429.4 362]]` against the pane's right edge at x 1264.\n\n## How tested\n- **New app suite `turn_pivot` (5):**\n  - the origin corner stays fixed, with undo and redo;\n  - zero is the pivot when no WCS is placed;\n  - after a preset, the point now on the origin stays, and the same angles are refused;\n  - the part-centre pivot equals the old behaviour;\n  - refusals by name.\n- **New UI tests (headless, real clicks):**\n  - `setup_align_tests::the_typed_turn_pivots_on_the_wcs_origin_by_real_clicks_and_undoes`: type Z = 90, Apply, Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y, switch to part centre, Apply;\n  - `setup_plane_tests::face_down_is_the_default_and_off_lays_the_face_up`.\n- **Updated** for the new defaults: the plane, points and `plane_face_lay` tests, and the structural test.\n- **Gate:**\n  - app: turn_pivot, setup_align, plane_align(_edges), points_align, axis_align, winding_align, setup_relative, setup_carry, carried_verify, setup_stock_source, rest_across_setups, commands_undo, project_roundtrip, setup_wcs and setup_sheet all pass;\n  - ui lib: 387 pass. The 1 failure is the known no-GPU `headless_run_succeeds` in the agent sandbox;\n  - clippy is clean. No snapshot PNGs were touched.\n\n**Not exercised:** a hands-on check in a fresh build.\n\nChangelog: Setups page: the Part alignment row's typed angles turn the part about the setup's WCS origin by default, keeping its place relative to the origin; an \"about\" choice beside Apply offers the part centre, and the presets still turn about the centre. \"Lay on a plane\" now lays a newly picked face (or three points) face down on the plane, with \"Face down\" / \"Points down\" on by default; saved projects are unchanged (#606)\n\nFixes #606\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
